<%# Grant rows for an orders role (Orders::GrantRows): any of these may act.
    Each row is a "Who" (a badge, the managers of a team, or the managers of
    the request's own team) and a "For" team. Without JavaScript every picker
    shows and one blank row is added per save. Locals: name (a key of
    Orders::SettingsEditor::GRANT_FIELDS), rows (Orders::GrantRows). %>
<div data-controller="orders-grant-rows">
  <div class="form-text mb-2"><%= Orders::SettingsEditor::FIELDS.fetch(name) %></div>
  <div class="form-text mb-2">Managers of a team: that team's own managers, not those of the teams above or below it. Managers of the request's own team include managers of the teams above it. A team under "For" covers the teams below it too.</div>
  <p class="mb-2">Any of these:</p>
  <div data-orders-grant-rows-target="list">
    <% rows.rows.each_with_index do |row, index| %>
      <%= render "orders/settings/grant_row", name: name, rows: rows, index: index, row: row %>
    <% end %>
    <%= render "orders/settings/grant_row", name: name, rows: rows, index: rows.rows.size, row: nil %>
  </div>
  <template data-orders-grant-rows-target="template">
    <%= render "orders/settings/grant_row", name: name, rows: rows, index: "NEW_ROW", row: nil %>
  </template>
  <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary" hidden data-orders-grant-rows-target="add" data-action="orders-grant-rows#add">Add a row</button>
</div>
